  "issue": 382,
  "request": "$senti.flow #382\n\nIssue #382: Make the command registry the single source of truth for help display.\n\nGoal: Generate top-level help, command help, and subcommand help from command registry / command class metadata instead of static help layouts and separated locale-only command descriptions.\n\nScope: Core senti CLI command registry, help display, command metadata, and plugin command metadata compatibility. Replace or reduce the static LAYOUT in src/help.js, align command entries/classes with help metadata such as section, summary, usage, args/options, experimental, and subcommands, and allow core and plugin commands to flow through the same help renderer.\n\nPolicy: Command registry / help metadata should live near command classes as static properties or methods. Command modules imported for metadata must avoid import-time side effects; heavy initialization belongs in run() or later execution timing. Avoid bloating plugin.json with command enumeration.\n\nOut of Scope: Full one-shot replacement of the flow lifecycle registry; flow can migrate gradually because it is tightly coupled to pre/post/onError/finally hooks.",
  "worktree": true,
